A radical symbol acts like parentheses to group operations. Any operations that appear under a radical should be performed before evaluating the root.

Simplify ~~\sqrt{6^2-4(3)}     

Approximate your answer to part (a) to three decimal places.


Explain why the following is incorrect:
			 \sqrt{6^2-4(3)} \amp = \sqrt{6^2}-\sqrt{4(3)}
				\amp = \sqrt{36} - \sqrt{12}
				\amp \approx 6-3.464 = 2.536

Find a decimal approximation rounded to two places.

-3+\sqrt{34}

\sqrt{6^2-4(3)}

